+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Ran from the workspace root on Node v24.14.0; exit code 0 with 'regression: all checks passed' after the seven assertion groups (collision integrity, post-collision migration, migrated-tail retention/idempotent re-read, malformed-line skipping, terminated-file stability, multi-buffer Unicode ordering with a >1 MiB fixture, non-session file untouched). The script imports only .prale-eval/subject.mjs plus node builtins, uses fixed timestamps and promise-ordered steps (no real time, randomness, network or credentials), writes all inputs under .prale-eval/scratch and removes them in a finally block; the scratch directory is gone after the run. Mutation check performed locally: reverting either source file alone to its faulty baseline made the same script fail with an uncaught AssertionError from node:assert/strict (no crash/import error/timeout), and the repairs were restored before this run. The workspace has no installed node_modules, so the repository's vitest suites could not be executed; that is the only unavailable optional validation dependency, and it is recorded here instead of being relied upon."
